  "query_preview": "..\nLook for dry and seasonable weather to continue on Thursday before\nan upper trough approaches the region to finish out the week along\nwith a surface cold front. Ensembles continue to keep much of the\nQPF southwest of the CWA. Thus, will maintain a dry forecast for\nnow.\n\nOver the weekend, upper ridging looks to rebound with dry weather\nconditions and warming temperatures. Highs across NE Montana for\nSunday will reach into the 50s and 60s. This will be short lived\nhowever, as the next cold front will bring in breezy conditions\nSunday night and cooler temperatures for Monday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM held the line for this forecast cycle with mostly dry weather\nconditions and little in the way of major temperature swings, save\nfor warmer temperatures on Sunday. Therefore, little in the way in\ndeviation was needed.",
